<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Privacy Policy - Endless Arrow</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --primary: #2563EB;
            --primary-dark: #1D4ED8;
            --surface: #FFFFFF;
            --bg: #F8FAFC;
            --text-main: #0F172A;
            --text-muted: #475569;
            --border: #E2E8F0;
            --card-bg: #FFFFFF;
            --badge-bg: #EFF6FF;
            --badge-text: #1D4ED8;
        }

        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            :root {
                --primary: #3B82F6;
                --primary-dark: #60A5FA;
                --surface: #1E293B;
                --bg: #0F172A;
                --text-main: #F8FAFC;
                --text-muted: #94A3B8;
                --border: #334155;
                --card-bg: #1E293B;
                --badge-bg: #1E3A8A;
                --badge-text: #93C5FD;
            }
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }

        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text-main);
            line-height: 1.65;
            padding: 24px 16px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 820px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 20px;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05), 0 8px 10px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.01);
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        header {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1E293B, #0F172A);
            color: #FFFFFF;
            padding: 40px 32px;
            border-bottom: 3px solid var(--primary);
        }

        .app-badge {
            display: inline-block;
            background: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2);
            color: #60A5FA;
            font-size: 13px;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 1.2px;
            padding: 6px 14px;
            border-radius: 20px;
            border: 1px solid rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.3);
            margin-bottom: 14px;
        }

        header h1 {
            font-size: 32px;
            font-weight: 800;
            letter-spacing: -0.5px;
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        header p {
            color: #94A3B8;
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        .content {
            padding: 36px 32px;
        }

        h2 {
            font-size: 20px;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--text-main);
            margin-top: 32px;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            padding-bottom: 8px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 10px;
        }

        h2:first-of-type {
            margin-top: 0;
        }

        p, ul, ol {
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 15px;
        }

        ul, ol {
            padding-left: 24px;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        strong {
            color: var(--text-main);
        }

        .info-card {
            background-color: var(--badge-bg);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);
            padding: 16px 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin: 20px 0;
            color: var(--text-main);
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        .info-card p {
            margin: 0;
            color: var(--text-main);
        }

        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin: 20px 0;
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        table th, table td {
            padding: 12px 14px;
            text-align: left;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
        }

        table th {
            background-color: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text-main);
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        table td {
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        a {
            color: var(--primary);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        a:hover {
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        footer {
            background-color: var(--bg);
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
            padding: 24px 32px;
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 13px;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        .contact-box {
            background: var(--bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .contact-box p {
            margin: 4px 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
    <header>
        <span class="app-badge">Official Policy</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p><strong>Application:</strong> Endless Arrow &bull; <strong>Effective Date:</strong> September 27, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="content">
        <div class="info-card">
            <p><strong>Summary:</strong> <strong>Endless Arrow</strong> is an offline-capable mobile puzzle game. We value your privacy. We do not require you to create an account to play, and we do not collect personal identifiers like your name, phone number, physical address, or contacts. This Privacy Policy details the information we handle to provide and improve the gameplay experience.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Endless Arrow</strong> ("we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, and discloses information when you use our mobile application (the "App"). By downloading, installing, or playing Endless Arrow, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.</p>

        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>We believe in data minimization. The app collects only what is strictly necessary to deliver puzzle mechanics, track your progression, and support the application:</p>

        <h3>A. Local Gameplay Data (Stored on Your Device)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Progress & Records:</strong> Completed level numbers, stars earned (1-3 stars), completion times, and high scores.</li>
            <li><strong>Game Preferences:</strong> Settings including sound effects volume, ambient music toggle, haptic vibration toggle, and dark/light visual theme preferences.</li>
            <li><strong>Game Items:</strong> Virtual hint counters and daily challenge records.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>All gameplay progress data is stored locally on your device via an encrypted SQLite Room database and is never transmitted to external third-party marketing brokers.</em></p>

        <h3>B. Automatically Collected Technical Data</h3>
        <p>When you access the game with an active internet connection, our third-party advertising partners and analytics frameworks may automatically collect non-personally identifiable technical information, including:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Device hardware model, brand, and manufacturer.</li>
            <li>Android operating system version and build number.</li>
            <li>Anonymous advertising identifiers (such as Google Advertising ID / GAID), subject to your device settings.</li>
            <li>Coarse network state (WiFi/Cellular connectivity status) to optimize ad delivery.</li>
            <li>General, non-precise location data derived from IP address (country or regional level).</li>
            <li>Aggregated, anonymous crash logs and diagnostic performance metrics.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Device Permissions & Purpose</h2>
        <p>Endless Arrow requests only minimal install-time Android permissions necessary for full functionality:</p>

        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Permission</th>
                    <th>Type</th>
                    <th>Purpose</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>android.permission.INTERNET</code></td>
                    <td>Normal (Install-Time)</td>
                    <td>Enables retrieving advertisements (banners, rewarded video ads for hints) and synchronizing cloud backup progress if enabled.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</code></td>
                    <td>Normal (Install-Time)</td>
                    <td>Checks whether the device has active internet access before attempting network calls, preventing app crashes when offline.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>android.permission.VIBRATE</code></td>
                    <td>Normal (Install-Time)</td>
                    <td>Provides physical haptic feedback when solving arrows, bumping obstacles, or long-pressing arrow trajectory guides. Can be disabled in Settings at any time.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>4. Third-Party Services & Advertising</h2>
        <p>Endless Arrow may integrate third-party software development kits (SDKs) to provide in-game advertising and analytics. These providers may collect information in accordance with their respective privacy policies:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Google AdMob / Google Mobile Ads:</strong> Used to display banner advertisements, interstitial level transitions, and rewarded video ads that grant optional puzzle hints. Google may use your device's advertising identifier to serve non-personalized or personalized ads depending on your consent and device settings.<br>
                Privacy Policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a><br>
                Ad Personalization Controls: <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://adssettings.google.com/</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Google Play Services:</strong> Provides core Android runtime libraries, app update notifications, and security integrity verification.<br>
                Privacy Policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Children's Privacy (COPPA & GDPR-K Compliance)</h2>
        <p>Endless Arrow is designed for general audiences and puzzle enthusiasts of all ages. We do not knowingly collect, solicit, or maintain personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13 (or under 16 in the European Union).</p>
        <p>If you are a parent or guardian and believe that your child has provided us with personal information without parental consent, please contact us immediately at <a href="mailto:ghazanfaredits95@gmail.com">ghazanfaredits95@gmail.com</a>, and we will promptly delete such information from our records.</p>

        <h2>6. Data Retention and User Deletion Rights</h2>
        <p>Because gameplay progress is saved locally on your device:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>In-App Reset:</strong> You can completely erase all local progress, stars, hints, and records at any time by navigating to <strong>Settings &rarr; Reset All Progress</strong> within the App.</li>
            <li><strong>App Uninstall / Clear Storage:</strong> Clearing app storage in your Android device settings or uninstalling the application permanently deletes all locally stored data.</li>
            <li><strong>Data Deletion Inquiries:</strong> If you have questions regarding any data handled by our third-party ad networks or wish to request data erasure, you may contact us at our support email below.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Security of Your Information</h2>
        <p>The security of your data is important to us. We employ standard industry safeguards to protect any data handled by the App:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>All network communications conducted by SDKs use Transport Layer Security (TLS/HTTPS) encryption in transit.</li>
            <li>Local application storage is protected by the Android sandbox security architecture, preventing unauthorized apps from accessing your gameplay records.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. International Data Transfers (GDPR & CCPA/CPRA Rights)</h2>
        <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have specific privacy rights regarding personal data:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>European Union / UK (GDPR):</strong> You have the right to access, rectify, or erase your data, restrict processing, and lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.</li>
            <li><strong>California Residents (CCPA / CPRA):</strong> We do not sell or share personal information for monetary value. You have the right to request disclosure of categories of information collected and opt-out of cross-context behavioral advertising via your Android OS device settings.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>9. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect modifications in our practices, legal requirements, or game features. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Effective Date". We encourage you to review this policy periodically.</p>

        <h2>10. Developer Contact Information</h2>
        <div class="contact-box">
            <p>If you have any questions, suggestions, or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy or your data, please contact the developer at:</p>
            <p><strong>Developer:</strong> Endless Arrow Team</p>
            <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:ghazanfaredits95@gmail.com">ghazanfaredits95@gmail.com</a></p>
            <p><strong>App:</strong> Endless Arrow (Android)</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer>
        &copy; 2026 Endless Arrow. All rights reserved. Complies with Google Play Developer Program Policies.
    </footer>
</div>

</body>
</html>
